387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 184 0 R
/T (Insertion Sort builds a sorted region at the front of the array. It takes the next element, shifts every larger element one place right, and drops it into the gap. The same way most people sort cards in hand)
/E (Insertion Sort builds a sorted region at the front of the array. It takes the next element, shifts every larger element one place right, and drops it into the gap. The same way most people sort cards in hand)
/Pg 19 0 R
